there are new allegations of racist  sexist and homophobic behavior against  two long-time cbs executives  who oversee the network's local tv  stations don champion a former freelance  reporter at our new york station wcvs tv  said in a facebook post that he was  bullied and discriminated against  for being a gay black man it follows  allegations of sexism and racism by  peter dunn and david friend at the cbs  station in philadelphia  first reported by the los angeles times  our national correspondent  arika duncan spoke to don champion about  experiencing what he calls  blatant bigotry my agent warned me  be careful you're gay black and a man  don champion says he was warned of  problems at wcbs tv in new york  before he started his job as a freelance  reporter in 2013.  you know i i i can't  i can't say enough how much fear you  live in  when you're in this situation whether i  was able to make  rent or eat that month was dependent on  how david felt about me  i was just trying to endure it and  survive champion came forward tuesday  after the release of an l.a times report  alleging sexism and racism by cbs  executives  david friend and peter dunn who run 28  local cbs stations  what's the biggest concern in all of  this  when you look at how long they have  yielded this amount of power how many  other  lives and careers they've ruined i mean  these are two  very very powerful men in the tv news  industry  the la times report focused largely on  cbs station kyw  tv in philadelphia the article reviewed  allegations that dunn and friend  cultivated a hostile work environment  that included bullying female managers  and blocking efforts to hire and retain  black journalists  margaret cronin was news director at kyw  for nearly two years  she left in 2017. cronin says friend  her boss at the time didn't explicitly  use racist language  but she says it was implied in some  emails  i would receive that when i was trying  very hard  to hire people of color  i seem to get them rejected left and  right  and i would get emails that say he can't  talk  or he can't write cronin told the times  that dunn reportedly took  aim at veteran anchor yuki washington  calling him  just a jive guy do you think peter dunn  and david friend are racist you don't  feel comfortable coming out and  answering that  do you think they should be fired i  believe they should no longer be  running the cbs television station  division what about the dozens of people  who've been impacted  by decisions made at the very top who  will never get  a chance to be yuki my heart goes out to  them  last night an emotional washington who  has been at kyw  more than 30 years thanked his  supporters my mom told me as a kid  that there is strength in numbers it's  still true we all have the power to  create change and we can do it  together cbs internally investigated  dunn in 2019  in a statement to the la times the  company said senior management at the  time addressed the situation with him  but had not had new complaints since  then earlier this week cbs announced  dunn and friend are on leave pending a  new  third party investigation adding cbs is  committed to a diverse  inclusive and respectful workplace in a  new statement tuesday the company said  all concerns presented will be  considered in the new investigation  when you hear of people now in powerful  positions at cbs saying we are  about diversity we respect everyone what  do you make of that  i have watched from the outside of the  changes at the network level  and i i certainly applaud that uh but  everyone in the in the tv business knows  that  from the local news level this was a  reckoning that needed to happen  friend previously told the la times that  he has a strong  track record when it comes to hiring  supporting and placing women and people  of color in  important roles and he also went on to  tell cbs news that champions accusations  are based on nothing but conjecture  friend offered champion of staff  job as a reporter and cb at cbs in 2019  which  champion did acknowledge friends said  his critiques of mr champion were always  based  on performance and had nothing to do  with race  gender or sexual orientation meanwhile  dunn's attorney tells cbs news that dunn  is confident  that he has always acted properly and  any investigation he says  will confirm this jerica  it's important as don said in your  reporting that this comes to light and  i'm so happy that it is uh and i saw the  outpouring of love for yuki  on social media yesterday you know just  once again cementing that he's not just  a hero to many in philly but all over  this country how's don doing  yeah he he really he really is uh vlad  and i just want to mention that because  i worked with yuki for several years at  that station  uh as for don you know he said that this  was a trigger for him and this is why he  decided to speak out  seeing that la times article and for him  reminiscing back to what he went through  he said made him want to  to call attention to his experience yeah  both yuki and don excellent reporters  thank you very much eureka as always we  appreciate it
 

